  <div class="web-project">

    <h2>ePortfolio Design</h2>

    <p>
      For the ePortfolio design assignment, I created
      two versions of my website. For the traditional
      version, I modified an existing HTML and CSS
      template using BBEdit. I customized the navigation,
      typography, and colors to reflect my professional
      identity as an academic librarian and the Palm
      Beach State College Libraries branding.
    </p>

    <h3>Traditionally Created ePortfolio</h3>

    <p>
      This website is my traditionally created ePortfolio.
      I adapted the provided template to include separate
      pages for my projects, added the PBSC Libraries logo,
      and incorporated PBSC's green-and-gold color scheme.
      I edited the HTML and CSS in BBEdit and published
      the website using GitHub Pages.
    </p>

    <h3>AI-Created ePortfolio</h3>

    <p>
      I also created an alternative ePortfolio using
      ChatGPT to generate the initial HTML and CSS.
      I wanted a more modern, single-page design while
      retaining the same PBSC branding. I used BBEdit
      to refine the generated code as I developed the
      website. The finished version includes project
      cards, links to my work, and expanded descriptions
      of the projects.
    </p>

